WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.505
There are thousands
upon thousands of Hindu temples in India.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:09.718
This one is special. Because in many ways

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:13.972
it is emblematic of how polarized
the country has become

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:16.975
under Prime Minister Narendra Modi.

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:21.271
And it is at the heart of his reelection
efforts.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.399
It has been three years
since the ground was broken

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:27.861
on the Ram Temple here in Ayodhya.

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:31.197
But the history of the site
is a lot longer

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:35.660
and more complicated than those numbers
suggest.

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:39.956
As India prepares
for a national election,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.543
the structure
on the banks of the River Sarayu

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:47.088
shows how Modi's Bharatiya Janata Party

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:52.594
has become a seemingly
unstoppable electoral machine,

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:55.847
and it could help Modi fundamentally

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:03.980
change the world's most populous country.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:08.026
Construction here in Ayodhya is nonstop,

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:12.489
as thousands of workers
race to complete the temple.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:18.119
The city in northern India has become one
of the most popular Hindu pilgrimage

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:21.372
destinations, and it has a significance

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:24.375
dating back thousands of years.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:30.006
That is when ancient scriptures
started citing it as the birthplace.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.341
of Ram.

00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:36.930
In Hinduism, Ram is one of the most widely
worshiped deities.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:41.851
He's a hero of one of the religion's
two epics, the Ramayana.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:47.649
Born a prince of Ayodhya, the tale recounts
his exile

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:50.735
and then his victory over
the forces of evil. 

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:54.489
He is seen as the embodiment of all that is
good.

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:57.158
The ideal man.

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:59.077
For all those reasons and more,

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:02.831
it is a convenient association
for the Prime Minister.

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:21.641
Modi has become India's
most powerful leader in decades

00:02:21.891 --> 00:02:25.687
by pushing Hindu nationalism or Hindutva.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.773
IIt is a strand of politics
that conflates Hindu

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.693
religious identity and policy. 

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:34.195
And it seeks to move India away

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:38.575
from the secular politics of its past,
instead forging 

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.452
a nation for the majority
Hindu population. 

00:02:41.452 --> 00:02:45.206
Ayodhya has become

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:49.752
a controversial focus of Hindu
nationalism.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.338
For the best part of 500 years,

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:57.051
the temple was the site of a mosque,
the Babri Masjid.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:59.179
In 1992,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:05.226
thousands of Hindus overwhelmed
security forces to demolish the mosque.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:09.355
It was a political earthquake
that saw thousands die

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.567
in the riots that followed.

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:21.659
The quest to build a new temple galvanized
the Hindu nationalist movement.

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:22.994
In his 2014 election

00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:27.707
campaign, he made a number of promises
to crack down on corruption,

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:31.544
develop the economy, introduce
a uniform civil code,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.631
end the autonomy of India's only

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:37.634
Muslim majority state, Jammu and Kashmir,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.555
and significantly build the Ram Temple.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.989
But the last decade in power
has been challenging at times,

00:04:00.114 --> 00:04:03.743
even as India's economy continues
to grow at a rapid rate.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:08.248
That growth hasn't benefited
everyone uniformly

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:12.418
and unemployed moment remains
stubbornly high.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:17.507
Modi has delivered
on some of his more contentious promises.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:22.637
Scrapping Kashmir's autonomy
and now building this temple.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.848
These are policies
that have helped Modi

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:29.727
overcome other electoral concerns.

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:30.687
Take the most

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:34.607
recent elections in November,
when key bellwether states,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:39.779
including Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan
and Chhattisgarh went to the polls.

00:04:39.988 --> 00:04:43.616
Opposition Leader Rahul Gandhi
and his Indian National Congress

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.869
had been hopeful of
capitalizing on

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:51.082
some of Modi's
perceived weaknesses to make inroads.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:55.712
There was a sense
before the vote that support among farmers

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:59.924
and women,
two of BJP's core constituencies,

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.844
might be waning.

00:05:13.396 --> 00:05:17.900
Neetu Patel is a former schoolteacher
who is now a homemaker.

00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:20.653
After years voting for the BJP,

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:25.033
she voted for Gandhi's
National Congress in November.

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:34.083
Patel was particularly

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:39.464
worried about inflation,
which remained high in November,

00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:43.676
For about 70% of India's rural households,

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:47.013
agriculture is still the sole livelihood.

00:05:47.096 --> 00:05:52.477
Modi promised to double farm income
when seeking his second term.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.606
Tulsiram Patidar
owns a large farm around Bhopal.

00:06:00.068 --> 00:06:02.987
Even so, it's taken

00:06:02.987 --> 00:06:07.492
and time for Patidar
to come around to Gandhi and the Congress.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:44.654
When the election
results landed on December 3rd,

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:48.116
the BJP retained power in Madhya Pradesh

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:51.202
and wrested control of the state
legislature

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:57.083
from the Indian National Congress
in both Rajasthan and Chattisgarh.

00:06:57.166 --> 00:07:00.628
The opposition political parties, despite
their best efforts, have not been able

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:04.674
to challenge or question Modi's
credibility in the eyes of the people.

00:07:04.882 --> 00:07:07.718
This is something which Rahul Gandhi
never understood, that holding

00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:11.264
a position of power
or holding a state office

00:07:11.347 --> 00:07:15.351
has a natural tendency
of introducing a charisma in you

00:07:15.393 --> 00:07:18.396
which has benefited Narendra Modi
in building up his profile.

00:07:18.521 --> 00:07:24.110
As concerns about unemployment
and corruption persist in some quarters,

00:07:24.193 --> 00:07:28.531
the Indian Prime Minister
has taken advantage of rising nationalism,

00:07:28.656 --> 00:07:31.826
which is also taking
hold in other parts of the world,

00:07:31.993 --> 00:07:35.955
and the Ram Temple stands
as an example of that.

00:08:08.237 --> 00:08:13.034
That Modi represents
the interest of all Hindus is, of course,

00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:18.080
hotly contested by his opponents,
not least Rahul Gandhi.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.708
There's nothing Hindu about what
the BJP does.

00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:22.543
They are not Hindu nationalists.

00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:24.837
They are nothing to do with Hinduism.

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:28.508
Since we are in a transition period
from the old fashioned

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:32.220
secular politics to a majoritian politics,
there are a lot of people

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:35.932
who are sympathizers
and supporters of the old ways.

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:38.809
They are very disturbed
by this political polarization.

00:08:38.809 --> 00:08:39.894
They think that, something

00:08:39.894 --> 00:08:44.190
fundamentally disruptive
is being unleashed by the present regime.

00:08:44.273 --> 00:08:47.902
The temple won't be completed
for a few years.

00:08:47.985 --> 00:08:52.823
And yet Modi is opening it in
January 2024,

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:56.869
just months before a general election.

00:08:56.953 --> 00:08:57.870
An electoral

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.082
victory might let his government pursue
an agenda

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:05.503
that could include more temples
on disputed sites,

00:09:05.586 --> 00:09:08.464
a national register of citizens

00:09:08.464 --> 00:09:12.051
and a law that makes it harder for Muslims

00:09:12.134 --> 00:09:16.347
to demonstrate
that they are Indian citizens,

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:19.725
steps that could cement India's move away

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:22.812
from the secular politics of its past.

